From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet: a result that is not a valid solid is a failure

Fillets that meet within the 2D tolerance (radii 2 + 1e-9 on a 4 wide face), fillets that meet
a finished fillet exactly (r = 5 after r = 5 on a 10 wide face) and fillets at the width of a
face on adjacent edges (r = 4 on a 4 wide face) were reported done with solids that BRepCheck
rejects (volume 333 for a box of 240).

Build() now checks the result with BRepCheck_Analyzer and reports the failure if it is not
valid. A result that is invalid only until SameParameter is applied to it, as callers do next
(DRAW test bug140), is accepted. The check is in the fillet API and not in
ChFi3d_Builder::Compute, which the chamfer builder shares: chamfers keep their results.

The check needs BRepCheck_Analyzer to return on every result the builder can produce. Four
fillets of r = 2 on a 4 x 4 face leave a face that is a point; the BRepTools_WireExplorer
change makes the check return on it, and the GTest covers that case under a deadline.

DRAW cases blend simple H8, Q3, Q8, W7, blend buildevol D8, blend complex B2 and the bugs
OCC25979 and OCC27711 (step 3) expected the faulty shape such a fillet returned; they now
expect the refusal and keep the old check for the day the fillet is built.

Related to #1568 and #1177.

Upstream: Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1669 (fork branch SecondMouseAU/OCCT fix/fillet-invalid-result-is-failure). This is the form of that
pull request as it stacks on the earlier patches of this series; where it differs from the pull request
as submitted it is only in the lines the stack made conflict (see Scripts/patches/README.md). The DRAW
test cases under tests/ that the pull request edits are not part of this patch: the build has no Draw.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepFilletAPI/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepFilletAPI/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet.cxx
index 8618984efb..b04008c3ea 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepFilletAPI/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepFilletAPI/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet.cxx
@@ -21,12 +21,14 @@
 #include <BRepAdaptor_Curve.hxx>
 #include <BRepAdaptor_Surface.hxx>
 #include <BRepAlgoAPI_Cut.hxx>
+#include <BRepBuilderAPI_Copy.hxx>
 #include <BRepBuilderAPI_MakeEdge.hxx>
 #include <BRepBuilderAPI_MakeFace.hxx>
 #include <BRepBuilderAPI_MakeWire.hxx>
 #include <BRepCheck_Analyzer.hxx>
 #include <BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet.hxx>
 #include <BRepGProp.hxx>
+#include <BRepLib.hxx>
 #include <BRepPrimAPI_MakePrism.hxx>
 #include <ChFiDS_ErrorStatus.hxx>
 #include <ChFiDS_Spine.hxx>
@@ -326,6 +328,18 @@ TopoDS_Shape pivotFillet(ChFi3d_FilBuilder& theBuilder)
   }
   return pivotCut(theBuilder.InitialShape(), aSpine->Edges(1), theBuilder.Radius(1));
 }
+
+//! True if the shape is valid, or becomes valid under the SameParameter pass callers apply next.
+bool isValidResult(const TopoDS_Shape& theShape)
+{
+  if (BRepCheck_Analyzer(theShape).IsValid())
+  {
+    return true;
+  }
+  BRepBuilderAPI_Copy aCopy(theShape);
+  BRepLib::SameParameter(aCopy.Shape(), Precision::Confusion(), true);
+  return BRepCheck_Analyzer(aCopy.Shape()).IsValid();
+}
 } // namespace
 
 //=================================================================================================
@@ -672,7 +686,8 @@ occ::handle<TopOpeBRepBuild_HBuilder> BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::Builder() const
 void BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::Build(const Message_ProgressRange& /*theRange*/)
 {
   myBuilder.Compute();
-  if (!myBuilder.IsDone())
+  // A result that is not a valid solid is a failure, as for a computation that failed.
+  if (!myBuilder.IsDone() || !isValidResult(myBuilder.Shape()))
   {
     // A fillet wider than its face has no start solution: see pivotCut.
     TopoDS_Shape aPivot;
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/GTests/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet_OppositeEdges_Test.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/GTests/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet_OppositeEdges_Test.cxx
index 5390e66a1a..926b3e0b8d 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/GTests/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet_OppositeEdges_Test.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/GTests/BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet_OppositeEdges_Test.cxx
@@ -30,7 +30,10 @@
 
 #include <gtest/gtest.h>
 
+#include <atomic>
+#include <chrono>
 #include <cmath>
+#include <thread>
 
 namespace
 {
@@ -92,6 +95,27 @@ TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1568_OverlappingOppositeFilletsAreNotAnIn
   }
 }
 
+// Radii that exceed the half width by less than the tolerance: the arcs meet within it. The result
+// is either refused or a valid solid, never a solid that is not one.
+TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1568_OppositeFilletsMeetingWithinToleranceAreNotInvalid)
+{
+  const TopoDS_Shape aBox    = BRepPrimAPI_MakeBox(4.0, 10.0, 6.0).Shape();
+  const double       aBoxVol = volumeOf(aBox);
+  for (const double anExcess : {1.e-12, 1.e-9, 1.e-7, 1.e-5})
+  {
+    BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet aFillet(aBox);
+    aFillet.Add(2.0 + anExcess, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(0.0, 5.0, 6.0)));
+    aFillet.Add(2.0 + anExcess, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(4.0, 5.0, 6.0)));
+    ASSERT_NO_THROW(aFillet.Build());
+    if (!aFillet.IsDone())
+    {
+      continue;
+    }
+    EXPECT_TRUE(BRepCheck_Analyzer(aFillet.Shape()).IsValid()) << "excess " << anExcess;
+    EXPECT_LT(volumeOf(aFillet.Shape()), aBoxVol) << "excess " << anExcess;
+  }
+}
+
 // Radii that add up to exactly the width: the arcs touch and the result is a valid solid.
 TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1568_OppositeFilletsThatTouchAreValid)
 {
@@ -106,3 +130,71 @@ TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1568_OppositeFilletsThatTouchAreValid)
   const double aRemoved = (1.0 - M_PI / 4.0) * (1.5 * 1.5 + 2.5 * 2.5) * 10.0;
   EXPECT_NEAR(volumeOf(aFillet.Shape()), 240.0 - aRemoved, 1.e-6);
 }
+
+// A fillet that meets a finished fillet exactly (r = 5 twice on a 10 wide face): either refused or
+// a valid solid.
+TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1177_SecondFilletThatMeetsTheFirstExactlyIsValid)
+{
+  const TopoDS_Shape       aBox = BRepPrimAPI_MakeBox(4.0, 10.0, 6.0).Shape();
+  BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet aFirst(aBox);
+  aFirst.Add(5.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(2.0, 0.0, 6.0)));
+  ASSERT_NO_THROW(aFirst.Build());
+  ASSERT_TRUE(aFirst.IsDone());
+  const TopoDS_Shape aRounded = aFirst.Shape();
+
+  BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet aSecond(aRounded);
+  aSecond.Add(5.0, findEdgeAt(aRounded, gp_Pnt(2.0, 10.0, 6.0)));
+  ASSERT_NO_THROW(aSecond.Build());
+  if (aSecond.IsDone())
+  {
+    EXPECT_TRUE(BRepCheck_Analyzer(aSecond.Shape()).IsValid());
+  }
+}
+
+// Two fillets on adjacent edges of a 4 wide face with r = w: never a solid that is not one.
+TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1177_AdjacentFilletsAtTheFaceWidthAreNotAnInvalidSolid)
+{
+  const TopoDS_Shape       aBox = BRepPrimAPI_MakeBox(4.0, 10.0, 6.0).Shape();
+  BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet aFillet(aBox);
+  aFillet.Add(4.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(4.0, 5.0, 6.0)));
+  aFillet.Add(4.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(2.0, 10.0, 6.0)));
+  ASSERT_NO_THROW(aFillet.Build());
+  if (aFillet.IsDone())
+  {
+    EXPECT_TRUE(BRepCheck_Analyzer(aFillet.Shape()).IsValid());
+  }
+}
+
+// Four fillets of r = w / 2 round the four edges of a 4 x 4 face of a cube: the arcs meet on the
+// centre lines and the face between them is a point. Build and the validity check must return, and
+// a reported solid must be valid. Both run on a thread under a deadline.
+TEST(BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest, OCCT1568_FourFilletsThatConsumeTheirFaceReturn)
+{
+  const TopoDS_Shape aBox = BRepPrimAPI_MakeBox(4.0, 4.0, 4.0).Shape();
+  std::atomic<int>   aState(-1); // -1 running, 0 refused, 1 built and valid, 2 built and not valid
+  std::thread        aThread([&]() {
+    BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet aFillet(aBox);
+    aFillet.Add(2.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(0.0, 2.0, 4.0)));
+    aFillet.Add(2.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(4.0, 2.0, 4.0)));
+    aFillet.Add(2.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(2.0, 0.0, 4.0)));
+    aFillet.Add(2.0, findEdgeAt(aBox, gp_Pnt(2.0, 4.0, 4.0)));
+    aFillet.Build();
+    if (!aFillet.IsDone() || aFillet.Shape().IsNull())
+    {
+      aState = 0;
+      return;
+    }
+    aState = BRepCheck_Analyzer(aFillet.Shape()).IsValid() ? 1 : 2;
+  });
+  for (int i = 0; i < 200 && aState.load() < 0; ++i)
+  {
+    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(50));
+  }
+  if (aState.load() < 0)
+  {
+    aThread.detach();
+    FAIL() << "the fillet did not return within 10 s";
+  }
+  aThread.join();
+  EXPECT_NE(aState.load(), 2) << "the builder reported a solid that is not valid";
+}
